WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.301 --> 00:00:03.336
How are you, buddy?
-I'm great, I'm great.

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.672
I've been --
I have a question for you.

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:09.308
How many people do you think
have peyronie's disease.

00:00:09.308 --> 00:00:11.778
-What's the disease?
-Peyronie's disease.

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:14.547
-Peyronie's? Yeah, I don't know.
-Have you seen ads?

00:00:14.547 --> 00:00:16.482
-I don't think I have seen
the peyronie's disease ads.

00:00:16.482 --> 00:00:19.619
-I've seen -- I would say I see
an ad for it maybe every hour.

00:00:19.619 --> 00:00:20.753
-Okay.
-I don't know if anyone --

00:00:20.753 --> 00:00:23.389
Does anyone else watch golf?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:23.389 --> 00:00:25.625
But it's a disease
I never knew existed.

00:00:25.625 --> 00:00:26.659
-Okay.

00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:28.961
-And they're very
high-budget commercials.

00:00:28.961 --> 00:00:30.730
Makes me believe it's an issue.
-Yeah.

00:00:30.730 --> 00:00:32.765
-And it's basically an issue

00:00:32.765 --> 00:00:38.137
where your penis has a very
dramatic angle to it.

00:00:38.137 --> 00:00:40.139
-You're being serious right now.
You watch --

00:00:40.139 --> 00:00:43.009
The Golf Channel has multiple
peyronie's disease ads.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:45.911
-It's just, like,
single packs of Viagra

00:00:45.911 --> 00:00:48.013
and peyronie's disease.
-Okay, got you.

00:00:48.013 --> 00:00:52.351
-And they demonstrate it
with a giant, like, an eggplant

00:00:52.351 --> 00:00:55.421
that has a bend in it
or, like, a full squash

00:00:55.421 --> 00:00:57.657
but it has a weird thing.
-Wow!

00:00:57.657 --> 00:01:00.526
-And I'm looking at it,
thinking, "What's --

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.128
Is this even a drug?

00:01:02.128 --> 00:01:04.831
This is like a little rubber
mallet that someone --

00:01:04.831 --> 00:01:06.866
-Do you think you're supposed
to eat the squash?

00:01:06.866 --> 00:01:09.502
-I feel like it's -- if that's
your issue, you're good.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:13.306
Like, it's not -- if you have an
eggplant, you don't need a drug.

00:01:13.306 --> 00:01:15.308
It's just like
a pat on the back.

00:01:15.308 --> 00:01:17.777
Like, "Get out there, buddy.
Have fun."

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:21.780
-But it must be --
it must affect golf.

00:01:21.780 --> 00:01:24.416
That seems to be the thing.
Maybe it's like some --

00:01:24.416 --> 00:01:25.751
it throws off your swing
if it's too severe.

00:01:25.751 --> 00:01:29.221
-Oh, yeah, yeah. Yeah.
If you have too big a dog leg.

00:01:29.221 --> 00:01:31.790
[ Laughter ]
And it makes you go left.

00:01:31.790 --> 00:01:33.192
[ Laughter continues ]

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.194
Anyway, that was
on my mind backstage,

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:36.763
but I can come back in
and start again.

00:01:36.763 --> 00:01:38.264
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.264 --> 00:01:39.498
-Well, it's not like --

00:01:39.498 --> 00:01:40.733
You don't have
that much else going on.

00:01:40.733 --> 00:01:42.168
So I understand why peyronie's

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:43.336
would be the first thing
we talk about.

00:01:43.336 --> 00:01:45.004
-The first thing.
-You had a baby.

00:01:45.004 --> 00:01:46.306
Congratulations.
-Yes. Thank you.

00:01:46.306 --> 00:01:47.574
-You had a baby boy.
-Yes.

00:01:47.574 --> 00:01:49.842
-Cosmo.
-Thank you. Yes.

00:01:49.842 --> 00:01:51.611
-Little baby Cosmo.
-Cosmo is a great name.

00:01:51.611 --> 00:01:52.912
I was very happy to hear it.

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:55.347
I think it, like, fits very well
with you and Scarlett.

00:01:55.347 --> 00:01:57.850
I think a Cosmo is just gonna
be perfect for the family.

00:01:57.850 --> 00:01:59.385
But how did you
come up with the name?

00:01:59.385 --> 00:02:01.420
-We were just assigned it
at the hospital.

00:02:01.420 --> 00:02:02.655
-Oh, really?
-Yeah.

00:02:02.655 --> 00:02:04.356
-That's a thing now?
-Yeah, people --

00:02:04.356 --> 00:02:07.126
I think the hospitals now
are just so overwhelmed

00:02:07.126 --> 00:02:08.661
that when the baby comes out,
they're just like,

00:02:08.661 --> 00:02:10.730
"Uh, that's Frank. Go."
You know, whatever.

00:02:10.730 --> 00:02:12.498
'Cause they're just --
I mean, so many people now

00:02:12.498 --> 00:02:13.799
are coming in, of course,
as you know,

00:02:13.799 --> 00:02:15.668
with the peyronie's disease.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.536
And so the hospitals are --
-Do you think --

00:02:17.536 --> 00:02:18.871
Can I ask you a question?
-Yeah.

00:02:18.871 --> 00:02:21.841
-Do you think de Blasio should
have locked down New York

00:02:21.841 --> 00:02:23.709
because of peyronie's?
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:26.178
-I mean, at some point,
businesses have to open up.

00:02:26.178 --> 00:02:28.047
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:02:28.047 --> 00:02:29.148
You know?
They gotta get back out there.

00:02:29.148 --> 00:02:31.684
-No matter how bad
the bend is --

00:02:31.684 --> 00:02:33.453
They're always like --
They're "flatten the bend."

00:02:33.453 --> 00:02:34.587
That's what they said.
-"Flatten the bend."

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.188
Yeah, that's --
Could we --

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:37.490
We could get that
trending tonight.

00:02:37.490 --> 00:02:40.326
[ Laughter ]
I don't know who I ask about --

00:02:40.326 --> 00:02:42.628
Who does your trends?
-What?

00:02:42.628 --> 00:02:44.597
I don't think anybody.
-Okay, all right, all right.

00:02:44.597 --> 00:02:45.765
-But that would be nice
to trend --

00:02:45.765 --> 00:02:47.366
"Flatten the bend."
-Yeah.

00:02:47.366 --> 00:02:50.636
-But -- so, baby Cosmo.
And now, it is a unique name.

00:02:50.636 --> 00:02:53.306
How did your family react?

00:02:53.306 --> 00:02:55.942
-My family
is very supportive, always.

00:02:55.942 --> 00:03:00.846
My mom, I would say,
was slightly thrown by it

00:03:00.846 --> 00:03:03.416
and didn't quite understand it.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:04.584
I don't know if she thought it
was kind of, like,

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:09.288
a hippy thing, but she --
You know, a dirty hippy.

00:03:09.288 --> 00:03:10.857
[ Laughter ]

00:03:10.857 --> 00:03:15.361
-That would be a nightmare.
-So negative.

00:03:15.361 --> 00:03:19.465
But I --
She would call us and say --

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:20.933
you know, like,
after three or four days,

00:03:20.933 --> 00:03:23.135
She'd be like, "Cosmo."

00:03:23.135 --> 00:03:26.372
She'd be like,
"And now, is it final?"

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:27.639
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.639 --> 00:03:29.708
"Like, did you submit
the birth certificate?"

00:03:29.708 --> 00:03:31.878
And we're like, "Oh, yeah,
we did that at the hospital,"

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:34.480
and she's like,
"Okay. Interesting.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.916
'Cause I was reading
that there's also a name

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:39.918
Cosimo, with an I.

00:03:39.918 --> 00:03:42.755
So that
could also be an option."

00:03:42.755 --> 00:03:44.457
Maybe you --"
-She preferred Cosimo?

00:03:44.457 --> 00:03:46.492
-She was like,
"Maybe you call him Cosimo,

00:03:46.492 --> 00:03:48.794
but then, you know,
that's his real name,

00:03:48.794 --> 00:03:51.230
but then,
you could call him still Cosmo."

00:03:51.230 --> 00:03:54.133
-What was the upside of Cosimo?
-I don't know.

00:03:54.133 --> 00:03:55.768
I don't know.
Because we live --

00:03:55.768 --> 00:03:57.136
You know,
she lives in Staten Island.

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:59.739
Eventually, she started
meeting various members

00:03:59.739 --> 00:04:03.542
of the Italian community who
have a lot of Cosmo relatives.

00:04:03.542 --> 00:04:05.844
And so then, she would call,
and she would say,

00:04:05.844 --> 00:04:09.916
"I met someone. They said
their uncle's name is Cosmo."

00:04:09.916 --> 00:04:11.250
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.250 --> 00:04:14.186
"So it is okay."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.186 --> 00:04:16.856
-I was like, "It's locked in."

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:21.160
Then she goes, "There's also
a patron saint called Cosmos.

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.829
So that's another option."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:27.734
"We don't need more worse
options, variants on Cosmo,

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.235
but thanks, Mom."
-Now it's officially Cosmo.

00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:30.436
-But now we did lock it in.

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:33.039
-And you are going --
This is very exciting.

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:34.673
This will be the first picture
anyone has seen.

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:36.342
-Oh, yeah.
We haven't shown anyone

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.277
a photo --
-I'm gonna put it over there.

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:41.514
-Yeah, he's a very,
very cute guy, and --

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:42.848
-Now, when did you
get this picture?

00:04:42.848 --> 00:04:44.584
'Cause I'm always fascinated.
Like --

00:04:44.584 --> 00:04:47.720
-I think this is probably
either the day he was born

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:50.189
or the first day home.
-Okay, gotcha.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.824
All right, let's take a look.

00:04:51.824 --> 00:04:54.293
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.293 --> 00:04:56.128
-And some --

00:04:56.128 --> 00:04:58.064
And the hair is coming in great.
-Yeah.

00:04:58.064 --> 00:04:59.632
-I mean, that's --
-I love that you --

00:04:59.632 --> 00:05:00.933
You know,
that thing about babies,

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:02.735
where you can't even tell
if they're like a boy or a girl.

00:05:02.735 --> 00:05:04.503
-Right, yeah.
We get that a lot.

00:05:04.503 --> 00:05:06.838
"Is it she? Is it..."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:06.838 --> 00:05:10.609
And we're like, "No, it's --"
-I see a lot of Scarlett.

00:05:10.609 --> 00:05:14.613
-It is -- I hate saying that,
but I do feel like I lost it,

00:05:14.613 --> 00:05:15.881
and it's mostly Scarlett.

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:17.816
You know,
I want to see myself, but...

00:05:17.816 --> 00:05:19.952
-Yeah.
-It's hard.

00:05:19.952 --> 00:05:21.387
-Did we talk about
your friendship with Che?

00:05:21.387 --> 00:05:24.556
You guys have a nice history
of giving each other

00:05:24.556 --> 00:05:27.293
bad gifts
as a show of affection.

00:05:27.293 --> 00:05:28.795
Did he give you a baby gift?

00:05:28.795 --> 00:05:33.666
-He, I would say --
was a more mature Che.

00:05:33.666 --> 00:05:35.768
-Okay.
-He got us a onesie.

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.469
A couple onesies.
-That's very useful, yeah.

00:05:37.469 --> 00:05:39.872
-Very practical, useful gift,
which was nice.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.874
He said,
"I'm sending you a onesie."

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:45.578
And then,
this was the onesie that he --

00:05:45.578 --> 00:05:49.915
-We got this one,
#DaddyIsOverParty.

00:05:49.915 --> 00:05:51.116
-Yep.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.116 --> 00:05:52.117
Yep.

00:05:52.117 --> 00:05:55.087
-And #CancelDad.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:55.087 --> 00:05:57.423
-Cancel Dad.
Yeah. Um...

00:05:57.423 --> 00:06:00.893
So that was really fun
to have your child wearing.

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:02.729
-Well, let's --
And remember, it looks --

00:06:02.729 --> 00:06:05.064
-Oh, yeah,
that's the completed look.

00:06:05.064 --> 00:06:06.933
[ Laughter ]

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:08.701
Oh, my God.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:12.204
The face
really matches the hashtag.

00:06:12.204 --> 00:06:13.539
-It's like --
Well, he is like,

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:16.808
"What did Dad just say?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.808 --> 00:06:18.177
-He --
It's so funny now.

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:21.580
Anything good that happens
in life, like having a baby,

00:06:21.580 --> 00:06:23.682
half the people --
Like, I posted --

00:06:23.682 --> 00:06:25.050
you know, posted a thing
about we had a baby.

00:06:25.050 --> 00:06:27.186
Half the comments are,
"Oh, my God, congrats,"

00:06:27.186 --> 00:06:29.922
and half are "Cancel Jost."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:29.922 --> 00:06:34.026
Because Che just gets
#CancelJost, like, trending,

00:06:34.026 --> 00:06:35.694
and then the people
who are saying congrats,

00:06:35.694 --> 00:06:37.763
then someone's like #CancelJost,
and the first person's like,

00:06:37.763 --> 00:06:39.565
"Why did -- Why?!
What happened?

00:06:39.565 --> 00:06:41.501
What did I miss?"
So he's a great friend.

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:42.568
-He's a good friend.
-He's a great friend.

00:06:42.568 --> 00:06:44.070
-If you're lucky
to have him by your side.

